Third-party provenance
======================

Rhombus/HOL is a direct Rhombus reimplementation of the HOL Light proof
engine. The repository intentionally stops the source-to-source port at the
engine boundary; the future surface language will be implemented with native
Rhombus macros rather than by porting HOL Light's parser, preterm, or printer.

HOL Light
---------

The engine modules under `rhombus/hol/` are direct or algorithm-preserving
translations of HOL Light sources, principally:

- fusion.ml -> fusion.rhm
- basics.ml -> basics.rhm
- nets.ml -> nets.rhm
- equal.ml -> equal.rhm
- bool.ml -> bool.rhm
- drule.ml -> drule.rhm
- tactics.ml -> tactics.rhm
- itab.ml -> itab.rhm
- simp.ml -> simp.rhm

The pinned source revision used for differential verification is
`cba9198db76e9dfb89cbd653df9412d01f65b22a`. The HOL Light copyright and
BSD-2-Clause terms are retained in `THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/HOL-Light.txt`.

OCaml
-----

`rhombus/hol/private/ordered_map.rhm` is a specialized translation of the
OCaml 4.14.1 standard-library map implementation, and
`rhombus/hol/private/hash_runtime.rkt` reproduces the relevant OCaml 4.14.1
runtime hashing behavior needed by the differential-compatible term map.

The OCaml 4.14.1 LGPL-2.1 terms and linking exception are retained in
`THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/OCaml.txt`.

